<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Privacy Policy - StudyMind</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <style>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      body {
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        background: #f8f9fa;
        color: #333;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .header {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
        color: white;
        padding: 40px 20px;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .header h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 32px;
        font-weight: 700;
      }
      .header p {
        margin: 10px 0 0;
        opacity: 0.9;
        font-size: 16px;
      }
      .container {
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 40px 20px;
      }
      .card {
        background: white;
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 24px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
      }
      h2 {
        color: #1a1a2e;
        font-size: 20px;
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }
      p {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        color: #444;
      }
      ul {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        padding-left: 24px;
        color: #444;
      }
      li {
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      strong {
        color: #1a1a2e;
      }
      .last-updated {
        text-align: center;
        color: #666;
        font-size: 14px;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
      }
      .contact-email {
        color: #667eea;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 500;
      }
      .contact-email:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      .footer {
        text-align: center;
        padding: 30px 20px;
        color: #666;
        font-size: 14px;
      }
      .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 20px;
        color: #667eea;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 500;
      }
      .back-link:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>StudyMind - Your AI Study Companion</p>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: April 2026</p>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>Welcome to StudyMind. This privacy policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. We believe in being straightforward about our data practices.</p>
        <p>StudyMind is a study app that helps you turn recordings, images, and text into organized study materials like notes, flashcards, and quizzes. You can use the app in guest mode without creating an account.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p><strong>Audio Recordings:</strong> When you record audio or upload audio files, the audio is sent to our server for AI-powered transcription. The audio is processed temporarily and the resulting text is returned to your device.</p>
        <p><strong>Images:</strong> When you capture photos of notes, textbooks, or whiteboards, or select images from your gallery, the images are sent to our server for text extraction (OCR). The images are processed temporarily and the extracted text is returned to your device.</p>
        <p><strong>Text Input:</strong> When you paste text from your clipboard, upload text files, or type content directly, that text is sent to our server for AI processing to generate study materials such as notes, flashcards, and quizzes.</p>
        <p><strong>Study Content:</strong> The study materials generated by the app (notes, flashcards, quizzes, and course organization) are stored locally on your device.</p>
        <p><strong>App Preferences:</strong> Settings such as your preferred language, notification preferences, and theme choice are stored locally on your device.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Where Your Data Is Stored</h2>
        <p><strong>On Your Device (Local Storage):</strong> The majority of your data lives on your device. This includes all study materials (notes, flashcards, quizzes), your course and topic organization, app settings and preferences, and notification schedules. There is no cross-device sync.</p>
        <p><strong>On Our Server (Temporary Processing Only):</strong> Audio, images, and text are sent to our server only when you use AI-powered features. This data is processed and the results are returned to your device. We do not permanently store your audio recordings, images, or text input on our servers after processing is complete.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use your information solely to provide the app's core features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Transcribe audio recordings into text</li>
          <li>Extract text from images of notes and textbooks</li>
          <li>Generate study notes, flashcards, and quizzes from your content</li>
          <li>Summarize text content you provide</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use your data for advertising, analytics, profiling, or any purpose other than providing the features you use within the app.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>StudyMind uses the following third-party services:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> Audio, images, and text you submit for AI processing are sent to OpenAI's API for transcription, text extraction, and study material generation. OpenAI processes this data according to their <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy" class="contact-email" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Play:</strong> In-app purchases and subscriptions are processed by Google Play. Payment information is handled entirely by Google and is never collected or stored by StudyMind.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with any other third parties.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
        <p>StudyMind can send study reminders as local notifications on your device. Notifications are entirely optional and are not enabled by default. You can enable, disable, or customize them at any time in the app's Settings. All notification scheduling happens locally on your device. No notification data is sent to our servers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>You have three options for deleting your data, available in the app's Settings:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Clear All Data</strong> (Settings &rarr; DATA section): Deletes all study data stored on your device, including semesters, courses, topics, notes, flashcards, and quizzes. Data stored on the server is not affected. This cannot be undone.</li>
          <li><strong>Delete My Data</strong> (Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Data): Permanently deletes all your study content from both the server and your device. Your account remains active but empty. This cannot be undone.</li>
          <li><strong>Delete Account</strong> (Settings &rarr; DATA section): Permanently deletes your account and all associated data from both the server and your device, including study content and purchase history. This cannot be undone.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can also request data deletion by contacting us at <a href="mailto:studymindv1@hotmail.com" class="contact-email">studymindv1@hotmail.com</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Your Rights and Controls</h2>
        <p>You have control over your data in the following ways:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Delete your data</strong> at any time using the options described above</li>
          <li><strong>Export your content</strong> as PDF or text files using the share feature on any study material screen</li>
          <li><strong>Manage notifications</strong> by enabling or disabling study reminders in Settings</li>
          <li><strong>Use guest mode</strong> without creating an account or providing personal information</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your information. Data transmitted between the app and our server is encrypted in transit. Study content stored on your device is protected by your device's built-in security features (screen lock, encryption). We do not store your audio recordings, images, or text on our servers longer than necessary to complete processing.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>StudyMind is intended for users aged 13 and older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, please contact us and we will take steps to delete that information.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time. When we make changes, we will update the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about this privacy policy or your data, please contact us at:</p>
        <p><a href="mailto:studymindv1@hotmail.com" class="contact-email">studymindv1@hotmail.com</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="footer">
        <p>&copy; 2026 StudyMind. All rights reserved.</p>
        <a href="/" class="back-link">Back to Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
